EXPERIMENT 2 – DATA SCRAPING
============================================================

AIM:
To extract tabular data from a web page using UiPath data-scraping or table-extraction activities and store the extracted data in a structured format.

PROCEDURE:
1. Open UiPath Studio and create a Process project named DataScraping.
2. Open Main.xaml and add a Sequence activity named Web Data Extraction.
3. Add a browser automation activity to open a website containing a structured table or repeated list.
4. Indicate the table or repeated data region using the extraction wizard.
5. Select the required columns.
6. Configure pagination or next-page handling if supported by the website.
7. Preview the extracted data and verify the column names and values.
8. Store the extracted result in a DataTable variable named scrapedData.
9. Add a Write Range activity to write the DataTable into Excel, or use Output Data Table to display it.
10. Run the workflow and verify the extracted rows and columns.
11. Save the project.

FLOW CHART:
[START] -> [Create DataScraping Project] -> [Add Sequence]
   -> [Open Website] -> [Indicate Website Table]
   -> [Select Required Columns] -> [Extract Table Data]
   -> [Store in scrapedData DataTable] -> [Output Data Table]
   -> [Write Range to Excel] -> [Verify Extracted Data] -> [END]


