EXPERIMENT 6 – IMAGE RECOGNITION
============================================================

AIM:
To use UiPath image-based activities to identify or interact with a visible screen element when reliable selector-based interaction is not available.

PROCEDURE:
1. Create a Process project named ImageRecognition.
2. Open Main.xaml.
3. Open the target desktop application or a sample window containing a stable visual element.
4. Add a Sequence activity named Image-Based Interaction.
5. Add an image-based activity such as Find Image or Click Image.
6. Indicate or capture the target image on the screen.
7. Adjust the matching area if required.
8. Configure a suitable timeout or retry strategy.
9. Use image highlighting or verification if available to confirm that the target was found.
10. Save and validate the workflow.
11. Run the workflow using the same screen resolution and display scaling.
12. Verify whether the target image was detected and clicked successfully.
13. Repeat the test after a minor screen-layout change to observe its limitations.

FLOW CHART:
[START] -> [Create ImageRecognition Project] -> [Open Target Application]
   -> [Add Sequence] -> [Capture Target Image] -> [Find Image]
   -> {Image Found?}
       YES -> [Click Image] -> [Display Success Message] -> [END]
       NO  -> [Display Image Not Found] -> [END]


