EXPERIMENT 7 – MULTI-BOT COLLABORATION
============================================================

AIM:
To design and test a workflow in which separate automation processes or robots perform different stages of a task and pass work between stages.

PROCEDURE:
1. Open UiPath Studio.
2. Create two separate Process projects named ProducerBot and ConsumerBot.
3. Prepare a small sample input dataset.
4. In ProducerBot, read or prepare the input records.
5. Save the records in a shared test location or publish work items using a supported queue approach.
6. In ConsumerBot, read the prepared records or retrieve the assigned queue items.
7. Implement the processing logic in ConsumerBot, such as validating records and writing their status.
8. Define the input and output formats clearly.
9. If Orchestrator is available, publish the processes and configure the required queues, assets, and robot access.
10. Run ProducerBot first and verify that the work items are available.
11. Run ConsumerBot and verify that each item is processed once.
12. Test a missing or invalid record and check whether the workflow handles the exception correctly.

FLOW CHART:
[START] -> [Prepare Input Dataset] -> [ProducerBot]
   -> [Read Input Records] -> [Publish Queue Items] -> [ConsumerBot]
   -> [Retrieve Queue Items] -> [Validate Records]
   -> {Record Valid?}
       YES -> [Process Record] --+
       NO  -> [Record Exception] -+
                                 |
                     [Write Output Status]
                                 |
                     [Verify Processed Records]
                                 |
                               [END]


