EXPERIMENT 9 – UIPATH AI FABRIC INTEGRATION
============================================================

AIM:
To integrate an available AI model or AI-powered service into a UiPath workflow and use its response in a simple automation task.

PROCEDURE:
1. Confirm with the instructor which AI integration, model endpoint, or supported package is available.
2. Create a Process project named AIIntegration.
3. Add a Sequence activity named AI-Assisted Processing.
4. Prepare a small, non-sensitive sample input, such as a text classification example.
5. Configure the approved AI integration or activity.
6. Store credentials in a secure asset or approved connection instead of hard-coding them.
7. Pass the sample input to the AI model using the required input fields.
8. Capture the model response in a suitable variable, such as a String.
9. Add validation or exception handling for empty responses and service errors.
10. Display the returned result using Message Box or write it into an output file.
11. Run the workflow with several sample inputs.
12. Compare the responses with expected results.
13. Save the workflow and record the integration, input, output, and limitations.

FLOW CHART:
[START] -> [Create AIIntegration Project] -> [Add Sequence]
   -> [Prepare Sample Input] -> [Configure AI Model]
   -> [Pass Input to AI Model] -> [Receive AI Response]
   -> {Valid Response?}
       YES -> [Store Response] -> [Display or Save Result] --+
       NO  -> [Handle Error] -> [Log Error] -----------------+
                                                             |
                                                       [Verify Output]
                                                             |
                                                           [END]


